      "body": "\nSummary:\nA model's state dict adapter is a class variable on the model class, so every\nrun of a model uses the same adapter. Some adapters only work with one\ncheckpointer.\n\n- Add an optional `state_dict_adapter_cls` field to `BaseModel.Config`. `None`\n  keeps the model class's `state_dict_adapter_cls`, so existing recipes are\n  unchanged.\n- Add `resolve_state_dict_adapter_cls`, and use it where training and the RL\n  initial load build the adapter.\n\nA recipe now pairs the adapter with its checkpointer explicitly:\n\n```python\nconfig.checkpointer = TorchCheckpointingManager.Config(...)\nconfig.model.state_dict_adapter_cls = SomeOtherAdapter\n```\n\nThe checkpoint conversion scripts are unchanged: they build model configs from a\nmodel name and flavor rather than a recipe, so the field is never set there.\n\nTest Plan:\nOn a devserver venv (torch 2.16.0.dev20261012+cu130, torch_checkpointing from GitHub main):\n\n`pytest -q tests/unit_tests/cpu/models/base/test_train_spec.py tests/unit_tests/cpu/components/checkpointer/test_checkpoint.py tests/unit_tests/cpu/models/test_state_dict_adapter.py tests/unit_tests/cpu/components/checkpointer/test_torch_checkpointing.py`\n\n```\n129 passed, 13 warnings in 48.54s\n```\n\n`pre-commit run --files <changed files>` passes every hook, including pyrefly.\n",
      "changedFiles": 5,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "fegin"
            },
            "body": "@ivy-zhou Per our discussion offline, it seems to be possible to merge the two different state_dict_adapter to one but the `StridedShard` case will be handled differently. If this is the case, we can just let state_dict_adapter takes a flag from checkpointer to know which checkpointer is enabled, then perform different paths for `StridedShard`. ",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-13T07:09:03Z",
            "databaseId": 6140275526,
            "updatedAt": "2026-10-13T07:09:03Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/5322#issuecomment-6140275526"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "ivy-zhou"
            },
            "body": "Sounds good... I think the challenge is that if we put such a config in the state_dict_adapter, the state_dict_adapter becomes aware of the checkpointer, but will defer to you guys here since either is a bit of a hack 👍 ",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-13T16:27:39Z",
